   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "58885410-128d-449c-ba5e-cb6f4fd2784d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 11. HTTP CACHE REQUEST DIRECTIVES\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8536dc8e-0925-4833-a2e6-b5cc5026c7a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "HTTP caching allows a client or intermediary server to store\n",
    "a previous HTTP response and reuse it for future requests.\n",
    "\n",
    "This can reduce:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Network traffic\n",
    "         ↓\n",
    "    Server requests\n",
    "         ↓\n",
    "    Response time\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "434bef53-11c3-4ee2-8c78-085a05a380bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "1. WHAT IS A CACHE?\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "A cache is temporary storage containing previously received\n",
    "HTTP responses.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "First request:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | GET /image.jpg\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Server\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | image.jpg\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Cache stores the response\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Later:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | GET /image.jpg\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Cache\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | Existing response\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Client\n",
    "\n",
    "The client may receive the response from the cache instead\n",
    "of contacting the server again.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "763b93e2-56aa-4e66-b66e-dcd697411589",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "2. WHAT ARE CACHE REQUEST DIRECTIVES?\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache request directives are instructions sent by the\n",
    "client to control how caches should handle the request\n",
    "and cached response.\n",
    "\n",
    "They are commonly sent using:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: no-cache\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "eca50df5-a498-4c19-9c92-204f8aab6ee2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "3. NO-CACHE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: no-cache\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "A cached response may exist, but it must be validated\n",
    "with the original server before being reused.\n",
    "\n",
    "Important:\n",
    "\n",
    "no-cache ≠ \"do not store\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead:\n",
    "\n",
    "    Cache may store response\n",
    "             ↓\n",
    "    Before reusing it\n",
    "             ↓\n",
    "    Validate with server\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | GET /data\n",
    "   | Cache-Control: no-cache\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Cache\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | Validate cached response\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Server\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | Valid / Updated?\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Cache\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Client\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "2ffd7ae8-eb49-49da-8d2b-4b4c7f21b6f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "4. NO-STORE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: no-store\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "Do not store the request or response in a cache.\n",
    "\n",
    "Flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | Request\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Server\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | Response\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Client\n",
    "\n",
    "The response should not be stored for later reuse.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE:\n",
    "\n",
    "no-cache\n",
    "    → Can store, but must validate before reuse\n",
    "\n",
    "no-store\n",
    "    → Do not store"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "f2448c9f-1270-4064-95ba-174eb6b0f00c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "5. MAX-AGE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: max-age=3600\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "3600 seconds = 1 hour\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "The client can use the cached response for up to\n",
    "3600 seconds while it is considered fresh.\n",
    "\n",
    "Flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "Response stored\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "   0 seconds\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "   Fresh\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "  3600 seconds\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "   Becomes stale\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Remember:\n",
    "\n",
    "max-age = How long the cached response can remain fresh\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "e132244d-a911-454d-8ce0-5cdb314beb0e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "6. MAX-STALE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: max-stale=600\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "The client is willing to accept a cached response that\n",
    "is stale, within the specified limit.\n",
    "\n",
    "Here:\n",
    "\n",
    "600 seconds = 10 minutes\n",
    "\n",
    "Simple idea:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Even if the cached response is slightly old,\n",
    "I can still accept it within this limit.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "cba8341b-2d7a-4039-a1b2-4c84b8e4550c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "7. MIN-FRESH\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: min-fresh=60\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "The client wants a cached response that will remain\n",
    "fresh for at least 60 more seconds.\n",
    "\n",
    "Think:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"I don't want a response that is about to become stale.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "a9c04388-376c-4439-bb55-90ad8bcd5c36",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "8. NO-TRANSFORM\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: no-transform\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "An intermediary/cache should not transform the content.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, an intermediary should not unnecessarily\n",
    "change the representation of the content.\n",
    "\n",
    "Simple idea:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Do not modify the content while handling it.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "ab223f89-a2ca-4cdf-ab32-dab9f83ff058",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "9. ONLY-IF-CACHED\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache-Control: only-if-cached\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "The client wants the response only from the cache.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cache should NOT contact the origin server to obtain\n",
    "a new response.\n",
    "\n",
    "Flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   | only-if-cached\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Cache\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   +---- Cached response exists\n",
    "   |          ↓\n",
    "   |        Client\n",
    "   |\n",
    "   +---- No cached response\n",
    "              ↓\n",
    "         Do not contact\n",
    "         origin server"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "3e1fce91-aee4-4297-b80b-1e35659a6833",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "10. COMPLETE EXAMPLE\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Request:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /products HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Host: example.com\n",
    "Cache-Control: max-age=3600\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "The client is specifying a caching preference using\n",
    "max-age.\n",
    "\n",
    "Another request:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /products HTTP/1.1\n",
    "Host: example.com\n",
    "Cache-Control: no-cache\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "A cached response can be stored, but it should be\n",
    "validated before being reused.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "11. IMPORTANT COMPARISON\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Directive       Meaning\n",
    "\n",
    "no-cache\n",
    "    → Store is allowed, but validate before reuse\n",
    "\n",
    "no-store\n",
    "    → Do not store\n",
    "\n",
    "max-age=3600\n",
    "    → Cached response can be fresh for 3600 seconds\n",
    "\n",
    "max-stale=600\n",
    "    → Client can accept a stale response within the limit\n",
    "\n",
    "min-fresh=60\n",
    "    → Client wants response fresh for at least 60 seconds\n",
    "\n",
    "no-transform\n",
    "    → Do not transform the content\n",
    "\n",
    "only-if-cached\n",
    "    → Use cache only; do not contact origin server"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "76ac9772-0f94-4e24-8c5e-ed2182d4783a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "MEMORY TRICK\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "NO-CACHE\n",
    "    → \"Check before using\"\n",
    "\n",
    "NO-STORE\n",
    "    → \"Don't save\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX-AGE\n",
    "    → \"How long can it stay fresh?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX-STALE\n",
    "    → \"I can accept slightly old data\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MIN-FRESH\n",
    "    → \"I want it fresh for some more time\"\n",
    "\n",
    "NO-TRANSFORM\n",
    "    → \"Don't modify it\"\n",
    "\n",
    "ONLY-IF-CACHED\n",
    "    → \"Cache only, don't go to server\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "SUMMARY\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "Cache request directives allow the client to communicate\n",
    "its caching requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "The main directives are:\n",
    "\n",
    "    no-cache\n",
    "    no-store\n",
    "    max-age\n",
    "    max-stale\n",
    "    min-fresh\n",
    "    no-transform\n",
    "    only-if-cached\n",
    "\n",
    "The most important distinction to remember:\n",
    "\n",
    "    no-cache\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "    Can store + must validate before reuse\n",
    "\n",
    "    no-store\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "    Do not store"
   ]
  }
 ],
